{"id": "en_tornado_home_p1", "total": 65.87, "segments": [{"text": "If a siren sounds at dusk, do not look outside to watch the dark cloud.", "start": 0.0, "end": 3.54}, {"text": "Jack has 2 minutes before a violent tornado strikes his sturdy suburban home.", "start": 4.18, "end": 7.4}, {"text": "Roaring winds hit early, smashing glass and throwing heavy debris through the windows.", "start": 7.92, "end": 11.38}, {"text": "Jack knows mobile homes and cars are not safe, so he stays indoors.", "start": 11.94, "end": 14.62}, {"text": "One. Go to the basement, or an interior room on the lowest floor with no windows.", "start": 15.38, "end": 18.86}, {"text": "Jack quickly enters the basement shelter, moving far away from the shattered windows.", "start": 19.48, "end": 22.64}, {"text": "Two. Put as many walls as possible between you and the outside storm.", "start": 23.18, "end": 26.48}, {"text": "He steps into the center of the basement, surrounding himself with solid walls.", "start": 26.48, "end": 29.84}, {"text": "Three. Cover your head and neck with your arms, a mattress or helmets.", "start": 30.54, "end": 33.44}, {"text": "Jack grabs a heavy mattress and covers his head and neck completely.", "start": 34.06, "end": 36.66}, {"text": "He drops into a tight crouch position under the mattress while winds howl.", "start": 37.16, "end": 40.12}, {"text": "The severe tornado destroys the upper house, but Jack remains protected underground.", "start": 40.64, "end": 44.22}, {"text": "Following every official safety rule kept him alive through the destructive storm.", "start": 44.78, "end": 47.84}, {"text": "He executed the survival steps perfectly inside his home while disaster struck.", "start": 48.28, "end": 51.72}, {"text": "It was the perfect plan, but there was just one unexpected problem remaining.", "start": 52.34, "end": 55.72}, {"text": "The violent winds tear the basement door off, exposing his safe shelter.", "start": 56.26, "end": 59.28}, {"text": "Heavy falling 